# T7b: editing a playing clip is ISR-safe. The clip engine reads its own copy of the playing clip
# (a double-buffer swap at a launch / loop boundary / reload), never the song the UI edits. Here a
# DRUMS clip plays while a hit is added on the grid; the clip keeps looping and the edited hit
# plays back, and the event stream stays sane.
wait 300
newsong 0
cursor 0 0
tap SEQ
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
tap HOME
tap SEL
tap PLAY
wait-bar 1
expect liveclip0 0
# re-open the grid and edit while it plays
tap SEQ
expect view 13
expect editclip 0
tapkey b0
tapkey w8
expect drumget0.0.8 1
events studio_clipliveedit_events.txt
wait-bar 3
expect liveclip0 0
expect drumget0.0.8 1
eventsstop
wait 1400
shot studio_clipliveedit.png
dump studio_clipliveedit.json
